From 51a4c4f11dbd08042f28e02d6fddc6484e766018 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:34:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] net: xpon: omci: serve real FEC counters in ME 312

The OLT creates a FEC PM history data ME and reads it with every PM
collection, but it had no counters behind it and read as zeros. Build its
15-min intervals on the same clock as ME 341, from the PHY FEC totals of
gpon_counters, through a new get_fec_counters op.

The totals are 32 bits wide and the agent samples them every minute, so an
unsigned difference survives a wrap; a generation bumped when the PHY
clears them marks a restart from zero. There is one PON line, so all
instances share the running counts.

Give the ME real attribute offsets: the closed interval lives in the
object, as in ME 341. Get on any other PM ME is unchanged, and so is the
MIB upload, which only carries the threshold data pointer.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
